# MASTER AI CODING PROMPT

## HU Fellowship Library — Church/Fellowship Book Borrowing & Summer Bible Study Notes System

You are a senior full-stack software engineer, system architect, UI/UX designer, database engineer, and QA engineer.

Build a complete, production-ready web application called:

# HU Fellowship Library

The application is a small digital library system for a church/Bible study fellowship. Members can browse books and **Summer Bible Study Notes**, borrow physical books, return them, and download digital/softcopy materials.

The system must be simple, clean, responsive, secure, and easy for fellowship members and administrators to use.

---

# 1. PROJECT OBJECTIVE

HU Fellowship Library manages books and study materials belonging to the fellowship.

The system must support two types of materials:

### 1. Hardcopy

Physical books that members can borrow.

Workflow:

```text
Register
   ↓
Login
   ↓
Browse Library
   ↓
View Book
   ↓
Request Book
   ↓
Book Becomes Reserved/Unavailable
   ↓
Admin Reviews Request
   ↓
Approve
   ↓
Member Borrows Book
   ↓
Member Requests Return
   ↓
Admin Confirms Return
   ↓
Book Becomes Available Again
```

### 2. Softcopy

Digital materials such as PDFs and EPUBs.

Workflow:

```text
Browse
   ↓
View Material
   ↓
Download
   ↓
Read
```

Softcopy materials do NOT require borrowing approval and do NOT affect physical availability.

