* Visible focus states
* Good contrast
* Accessible buttons
* Meaningful error messages

Do not rely only on colors to communicate status.

---

# 63. AUTHENTICATION

Use JWT authentication.

Passwords must be hashed using bcrypt.

Never store:

```text
plain-text passwords
```

JWT should contain appropriate user identification/role information.

Protect routes using authentication middleware.

---

# 64. ROLE-BASED ACCESS CONTROL

Members must NOT be able to access:

```text
/admin/*
```

Members must NOT be able to:

* Approve requests
* Reject requests
* Add books
* Delete books
* Manage categories
* Manage members
* Confirm returns

Backend authorization must enforce this even if someone manually calls the API.

Never rely only on frontend route protection.

---

# 65. VALIDATION

Validate on both:

```text
Frontend
Backend
```

Examples:

Email:

```text
valid email format
```

Password:

```text
minimum reasonable length
```

Phone:

```text
valid expected format
```

Publication year:

```text
valid year
```

Quantity:

```text
positive integer for hardcopy
```

Softcopy:

```text
valid file required
```

---

# 66. ERROR HANDLING

Use consistent API responses.

Example:

```json
{
  "success": false,
  "message": "Book is currently unavailable."
}
```

Success:

```json
{
  "success": true,
  "message": "Book request submitted successfully."
}
```

Frontend should display meaningful error messages.

Avoid exposing database errors directly to users.

---

# 67. LOADING STATES

Every important async operation should have loading feedback.

Examples:

```text
Loading books...
Submitting request...
Approving request...
Uploading file...
Saving...
```

Use disabled buttons while appropriate operations are processing.

---

# 68. EMPTY STATES

Create useful empty states.

Example:

```text
No books found.

Try changing your search or category filter.
```

No requests:

```text
You have no borrowing requests yet.
```

No borrowings:

```text
You currently have no active borrowings.
```

---

# 69. SECURITY

Implement:

* bcrypt password hashing
* JWT authentication
* Role-based authorization
* Parameterized SQL queries
* Backend validation
* Safe file uploads
* MIME validation
* File size restrictions
* CORS configuration
* Environment variables
* Secure error handling

Never expose:

```text
JWT_SECRET
DB_PASSWORD
private environment variables
```

to the frontend.

