# 102. FINAL INSTRUCTION TO THE AI CODING AGENT

Do not merely create a mockup.

Build the actual working application.

The frontend, backend, database, authentication, APIs, file uploads, borrowing workflow, reservation logic, admin management, and responsive UI must work together.

Do not fake data in the final application.

Do not implement important business rules only on the frontend.

The backend and database must enforce the rules.

Pay particular attention to the hardcopy reservation transaction because two members may attempt to request the last available copy at the same time.

The system must maintain consistent availability.

The final application identity must be:

# HU Fellowship Library

with the uploaded HU Fellowship logo as the official logo.

The main Bible-study category must be:

# Summer Bible Study Notes

The final experience should feel like a **real, simple, modern fellowship library**, not a generic CRUD demonstration.

Build it systematically, test every major workflow, fix errors, and provide complete setup instructions when finished.
